WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:07.529
Frederick Douglas had this great quote, "I
shall always unite with those who do good,

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:10.610
but I shall not unite with those who do wrong."

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:17.480
I wish this person could be alive today to
be an example of what kids can be and do.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:23.710
If they have the drive to conceive of a dream
and the guts and the strength and the motivation

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:30.140
to achieve that dream, we want to be part
of the resources that help them receive that

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.140
dream.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.140
And that's my biggest hope.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:38.760
I think that to invest in kids that can become
great from Hillsdale is really to invest in

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.489
the future of our country.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:43.760
You know, my grandparents were tremendously
philanthropic.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:50.300
They talked about the importance of helping
others that can't otherwise afford to do things

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.420
that are important.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.840
The emphasis in my father's teaching was invest
in other people.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.930
Don't just keep it all for yourself.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:03.290
My specialty is working with terminally ill
adults and children in grief therapy.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.800
I actually was led to that because when I
was thirteen years old, I was diagnosed with

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.800
Muscular dystrophy.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.260
It was a misdiagnosis.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:14.570
I was in a wheelchair and effectively blind
because my muscles were not strong enough

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.270
to see straight forward.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:19.470
Came to Detroit and there it was found that
I was misdiagnosed.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:23.640
So I felt I had gotten my life back and I
am confident that that had a great deal of

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.860
influence on my direction.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.560
I love my private practice.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.130
People ask me how can I hold somebody in my
arms when they die, and say, I could never

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.130
do that.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.460
I could never be an accountant.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:40.970
I do believe my experiences as a child--understanding
that I was not going to be living very long--has

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:45.680
really helped me to become very comfortable
helping others to die.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.280
Into Michigan, when I had my first call from
McCormick Theological Seminary.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.550
I met Bonnie there and she claims that I promised
her a ticket to heaven.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:56.960
In truth, I'm the one who got that ticket,
I think, because we've been married thirty-four

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:02.130
years, and I'm married to my best friend and
I'm still stupidly in love with her, so it's

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.130
cool.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.450
Bonnie is an alum, our daughter Hillary went
to Hillsdale, too.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:10.369
She got a degree in psychology and now she
is working in philanthropic work as well.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:16.640
The thing that makes Hillsdale Hillsdale are
the students that aspire to go there and to

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.750
do great things.

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:21.060
That's really what our interest has been.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:25.420
Hopefully, to support students, especially
those who otherwise couldn't afford to go

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:26.420
there.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.030
I love Hillsdale College.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.610
I think that school is one of the most amazing
resources in America.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.371
I've always told my wife, "Doggone it, I wish
I had graduated from this school."

